  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\n[`Window.customElements`](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/custom-elements.html#dom-window-customelements) is not null according to the IDL, but it now returns the associated Document's custom element registry which [can be null](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#document-custom-element-registry):\n> Each [document](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document) has a... custom element registry (null or a [CustomElementRegistry](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/custom-elements.html#customelementregistry) object)\n\nIn some places the spec assigns the Document's CustomElementRegistry when constructing it. ([1](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/document-sequences.html#creating-browsing-contexts:document-custom-element-registry) [2](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/document-lifecycle.html#shared-document-creation-infrastructure:document-custom-element-registry)) But I don't know if that's all the places. Either way, this needs some clarification.\n\n@annevk ",
